# StressFlow – Controlled CPU & RAM Load Orchestrator

## Overview

StressFlow is a simple project I built to test how a system behaves under controlled CPU and memory load.
It uses multiple Python scripts that run one after another with a fixed delay, instead of hitting the system all at once.

The idea is to simulate a more realistic load pattern — gradually increasing pressure, then shutting things down in the same controlled way. Everything is logged so you can clearly see what started and stopped, and when.


## Features

* Runs 6 stress scripts (CPU + RAM) in sequence
* Adds a delay between each step (default: 1 minute)
* Stops everything in the same order it started
* Logs all activity with timestamps
* Runs inside a single Docker container
* Easy to tweak depending on your testing needs


